User Story 1: Recording Bank Transfer Payment
ID: SA-ACC-01
Priority: High
Risk: Medium
Estimate: 5 Story Points

Narrative: As an accounting staff member, I want to manually record a bank transfer payment received from a merchant, so that their outstanding debt is reduced and their purchasing power is restored.

Acceptance Criteria:
System must allow selection of a merchant account via a searchable list or unique business ID
System must capture the payment amount, the bank reference number, and the date of the transfer
Upon saving, the merchant’s current debt must be decreased by the payment amount in real-time
The system must automatically recalculate and update the merchant’s "available credit" field

User Story 2: Recording Cheque Payment
ID: SA-ACC-02
Priority: Medium
Risk: Medium
Estimate: 3 Story Points

Narrative: As an accounting staff member, I want to log a cheque payment into the system, so that the merchant’s account balance accurately reflects physical funds received.

Acceptance Criteria:
System must provide a specific "cheque" payment type option within the payment entry interface
System must require the entry of a cheque number and the name of the issuing bank
The payment must be linked to the merchant's profile to ensure the ledger remains balanced
The system must generate a unique internal transaction receipt number for auditing purposes

User Story 3: Recording Card Payment
ID: SA-ACC-03
Priority: High
Risk: Medium
Estimate: 5 Story Points

Narrative: As an accounting staff member, I want to enter card transaction details for a merchant payment, so that the financial records are reconciled and the merchant's account status is updated.

Acceptance Criteria:
System must allow the entry of a card transaction authorization code from the external payment gateway
System must validate that the payment amount is a positive numerical value before processing
The system must trigger a status check to move the account from "suspended" to "normal" if the debt falls below the required threshold
The transaction must be recorded in a permanent financial audit trail

User Story 4: Generating Merchant Financial Statements
ID: SA-ACC-04
Priority: Medium
Risk: Low
Estimate: 8 Story Points

Narrative: As an accounting staff member, I want to generate a financial statement for a specific merchant, so that I can provide them with a summary of their orders and payments for a specific timeframe.

Acceptance Criteria:
System must allow the user to define a "start date" and "end date" for the statement period
The statement must list all individual invoices (orders) and all recorded payments (bank/card/cheque) chronologically
The system must calculate and display the total opening balance, total period activity, and final closing balance
The resulting report must be viewable on-screen with an option to export as a PDF document
